dcb@wdl1.wdl.loral.com (David C Blume) writes:

>My question is:  If you get a wish EARLY in the game -- when you're in
>need of good armor AND weapons- would you wish for the weapon or the armor?

Since the key to winning Nethack is NOT DIEING, I would recommend getting
good armour ahead of a good weapon. Get something which aids you in actually
surviving, as opposed to being a more efficient killer.

With this in mind, first on the list would be blessed speed boots. You could get
gray dragon scale mail, but invariably you find a splint/banded/plate mail
somewhere in the first few levels, which does a pretty good job. A shield of
reflection is pretty handy, particularly if you have a few ray wands, but I
wouldn't waste a wish on it early on. Same for cloaks (invisible or
displacement).  Digressing slightly, there was some argument a while ago about
which was better to have, displacement or invisible. I don't recall anyone
giving this answer, which is; HAVE BOTH! Wear your cloak of displacement, and
quaff a blessed potion of invisibility to gain permanent invisibility. It makes
it mighty difficult for monsters to hit you, and very easy to run away (even if
you don't have speed).

My preference for armour is based largely on experience, since I used to always
wish for Stormbringer early on, and invariably got killed by a swarm of killer
bees, or soldier ants, or got frozen by a floating eye and ended up being
nibbled to death by a gecko, or......
A good weapon is great to have, but not as essential as good armour.

